description:
Design a clock divider that generates a square wave signal with a frequency of approximately 441 kHz from an input clock signal. The module has a reset input to initialize the counter and the output signal, and it counts clock cycles until it reaches a predefined count (1134 cycles), at which point it toggles the output signal (cs) and resets the counter. This effectively creates a pulse output that can be used for various timing applications in digital circuits.
module top_module(
    input wire clk,
	 input wire reset,
	 output reg cs
	 );

code:
module top_module(
    input wire clk,
	 input wire reset,
	 output reg cs
	 );reg [10:0] cuento; 


always @(posedge clk,posedge reset) 
begin
	if (reset) 
	begin
		cs <= 0;
		cuento <= 0;
	end 
	else 
	begin		
		if (cuento == 11'd1133) 
		begin                    
			cuento <= 11'h000;      
			cs <= ~cs;  
		end 
		else 
			cuento <= cuento + 1'b1; 
	end
end

endmodule

