description:
Design a 4x4 matrix multiplier that takes two 4x4 matrices, A and B, as 16-bit inputs and produces their product, C, as a 16-bit output. The module iteratively computes the sum of the products of respective elements from the input matrices, structured within a nested loop to handle multiplication and accumulation for each matrix position. The resulting 4x4 matrix is mapped back into a single dimensional output, enabling efficient matrix operations within a digital circuit.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] A,
    input [15:0] B,
    output reg [15:0] C
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] A,
    input [15:0] B,
    output reg [15:0] C
);reg [3:0] i, j, k;
reg [15:0] sum;

always @* begin
    for(i = 0; i < 4; i = i + 1) begin
        for(j = 0; j < 4; j = j + 1) begin
            sum = 0;
            for(k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) begin
                sum = sum + A[i*4 + k] * B[k*4 + j];
            end
            C[i*4 + j] = sum;
        end
    end
end

endmodule

