Design a D flip-flop with positive edge-triggered clocking. The module takes input data (D) and, on the rising edge of the clock (CLK), captures the input value and stores it in an internal register (Q_reg). The stored value is then output to Q, creating a sequential element that retains the last captured input until the next clock event. The module also includes power and ground connection inputs for operation within a specific power supply system.
module top_module(
    //# {{data|Data Signals}}
    input  D   ,
    output Q   ,

    //# {{clocks|Clocking}}
    input  CLK ,

    //# {{power|Power}}
    input  VPB ,
    input  VPWR,
    input  VGND,
    input  VNB
);

